Serves 4–5
Cooking time: ~2–2.5 hours

Rich, aromatic broth with tender beef 🍜🤍

⸻
INGREDIENTS

Beef &amp; Base
• 1 kg beef shank, cut into 2-inch chunks
• 2 tbsp oil
• 3–4 slices ginger
• 3 cloves garlic
• 2 scallions, cut into ~5 cm pieces
• 1 onion, cut into wedges
• 1 tomato, cut into chunks
• 1 tbsp tomato paste
• 1-2 tbsp chilli bean sauce (Toban Djan) OR chilli oil of choice

Broth &amp; Seasoning 
• 1 tsp sugar
• 60g soy sauce (mix light + dark soy sauce 1:1)
• 60g Shaoxing wine
• 3 bay leaves
• Mixed spice (2 star anise, 1 cinnamon stick, 3 cloves, 1 tsp coriander seeds, 1 black cardamom pod, 1/2 tsp fennel seeds) - IT’S OKAY TO MISS SOME
• 1/2 tsp five-spice powder
• 1/2 tsp pepper

To Serve
• Noodles of choice
• Bok choy
• Pickled mustard greens (optional)
• Extra chili oil

⸻
INSTRUCTIONS

1️⃣ Blanch the Beef
Place the beef in a pot with water, 2 slices of ginger, and a splash of Shaoxing wine.
Bring to a boil for 5 minutes to remove impurities.
Drain the beef, rinse it under running water. Set the cleaned beef aside.

2️⃣ Toast the Aromatics &amp; Spices
(Optional) Toast the dry spices on a pan over low heat for 1-2 minutes until aromatic. Transfer them to a spice bag or tea filter to use later.

In the same pan, heat 2 tbsp oil over medium heat.
Add ginger, garlic, scallions, onion, and tomato.
Cook until fragrant and softened.
Add chili paste (or chili oil) and tomato paste, then cook for 2–3 minutes to deepen the flavor.

3️⃣ Build the Broth
Return the beef to the pot.
Add sugar, soy sauce, Shaoxing wine, and enough water to cover the beef.

Add the spice bag, bay leaves, five-spice powder, and black pepper.
Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low.

4️⃣ Slow Simmer
Cover and simmer for 1.5–2 hours, until the beef becomes very tender and the broth rich and aromatic. Taste &amp; adjust the seasoning to your liking.

5️⃣ Prepare Noodles &amp; Vegetables
Cook noodles according to package instructions.
Blanch bok choy in boiling water for 60s or until tender.
Place noodles &amp; bok choy in a bowl.
Ladle the hot broth &amp; meat over the noodles.
Add pickled mustard greens and extra chili oil if desired.

